/*
Problem: A Number After a Double Reversal (LC 2119)
Topic: Math

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Reversing a number removes its leading
zeros.

If a number ends with zero (and is not
0 itself), the first reversal loses
those trailing zeros permanently.

After reversing again, the original
number cannot be recovered.

Therefore:

• num = 0      -> true
• num ends in 0 -> false
• Otherwise     -> true

--------------------------------------------------

Time: O(1)

Space: O(1)

--------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    bool isSameAfterReversals(int num) {

        if(num % 10 == 0 && num != 0)
            return false;

        return true;
    }
};
